{"kind":"request","text":"Design amendment to notes/2026-10-19-self-hosting-on-celld.md: the Git host becomes the deployer's choice, `none`, `artifacts` or `github.com`, and a deployment with host `none` degrades to a room without publication. Hugh agreed this direction on 2026-10-27 for a local self-hosted deployment on one Mac mini (celld, one node, a local bucket). Write a design note, or a new draft of the self-hosting note, and land it after checker review.\n\nWhy: the 2026-10-19 note makes dap's own bounded Git host (host `self`, slice H2, request a3460956) the default for self-hosting. For a local-only deployment, a deployer may want no Git host at all. `none` is less to build and less to run than H2, and it does not hide the cost: the record then lives in one place.\n\nToday's behaviour (main aa3ae873): the register records `host` and `namespace` at install and never changes them (docs/hosts.md). A register whose host is not configured gets no outside port, and its operations stay recorded and unsent. `dap claim` and `dap create` wait until the destination is created and confirmed, so with no host, creation never finishes. The CLI defaults `--host` to `github.com` (packages/cli/src/commands.ts:497).\n\nWhat the note needs to decide:\n1. Install: `dap install --host none`, recorded on the register like any other host.\n2. Creation: the directory creates membership and the rules scope, and either no destination or a destination with no repository. State which, and what the room page and `dap status` show.\n3. Refusals: each act that needs a repository (publication, `read-token` and `dap clone`, `dap remote`, a change lane's merge to a publication, the archive binding, the rules-tree certificate if it is a destination operation) is refused with one clear reason, never left pending.\n4. What keeps working, as a witness list: create, members, invitations, acts and rules, the page, MCP, retained files kept in the scope or the bucket, `dap verify --all`.\n5. Whether a `none` room can attach a Git host later. Today the register's host is fixed. No backward compatibility is required.\n6. `artifacts` is available only on the Cloudflare runtime, through the Workers binding. On celld the choices are `none` and `github.com`. Say whether Artifacts can be reached from outside Cloudflare, or record that it cannot.\n7. Durability: with `none`, the second place of the record (docs/architecture.md, \"Durability: three places the record lives\") is absent. Say what the operator's backup must then cover.\n8. Where H2 goes: kept as a later option, re-ordered, or superseded. Revise H1 99918e60 if its scope changes.\n9. Kernel placement under the coherence filing rule: new versions of the register and directory definitions count toward K1. Name the K item or say why none applies.\n\nRelated: a SeaweedFS evaluation on the Mac mini, as the local bucket for celld, runs now in Hugh's session. Its results go into a note of their own and inform section 4.7 (record and backup) of the self-hosting note.","body":{"conditions":"A design note or a new draft of notes/2026-10-19-self-hosting-on-celld.md that decides items 1 to 9, approved by the checker and landed on main; status lines updated per the design-note status convention.","target":"inherit","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}